 "power_notes": "Track widths here are sized for the tracks that remain: plane taps and short stubs. The main currents ride on copper the width rules can't see: VBUS_IN/VBUS/PVDD/+3V3 on In2 plane regions plus F.Cu pours, and the amp OUT/SPK nets (3.7 A rms continuous sine, 2 x 56 W governor-capped) on the solid fan-in pours from kicad/gen/power_zones.py. check_irdrop covers those paths at P8. +5V is budgeted at 1.1 A, what the SY8303 delivers at the worst case of its loads: the SY8089 3V3 buck's input at the +3V3 budget of 0.8 A (ESP32 radio peaks; 3.3 x 0.8 / (0.88 x 5.0) = 0.60 A), LP5907 3V3A 0.10 A, +5VA 0.05 A, two TPA3221 VDD/GVDD/AVDD 0.10 A, the ultra-front board over J3 0.15 A and the CH340C 0.02 A (1.02 A). The trunk from L9 to U5's VIN is 0.58-0.60 mm, past the 0.56 mm that 1.1 A needs at dT=10, and BUCK5_LX carries the same 1.1 A. Every other +5V track is a branch off that trunk and sits in an override at 0.4 A: by a DC solve of the routed copper the most any branch carries is 0.29 A (amp A, CH340C and the front board, west), and the buck output caps' (C13/C14) and the 3V3 buck's input cap's (C15) ripple stays under 0.4 A rms; 0.35 mm tracks carry 0.7 A, so the branches have margin. No override circle reaches a trunk segment's midpoint.",
 "diff_pairs_note": "Explicitly empty. The USB full-speed pair (12 Mb/s) and the two 100BASE-TX pairs run about 10 mm, so coupling them adds nothing measurable, and the router doesn't couple pairs (route_critical's KRT diff pass shorted). They are routed as ordinary nets at the Default width."
}